# The default UK keymap, key by key (apps/desktop/PLAN.md "Keyboard mapping").
# F-row: F9 = Note (to d1's n pattern; adds # n "0"), pads enter numbers
F9 last
# pads: Q = 0 (second row starts at 0), T = 4, I = 7; - = pad 11 = -2
Q +100 T +100 I +100 - last
# a chord: keys down within the chord window (40 ms) stack
+100 down:Q +10 down:T +10 down:I +10 up:Q up:T up:I last
# rolled over, but more than 40 ms apart: separate steps
+100 down:A +100 down:S +10 up:A up:S +100 last print
# Shift passes through: Shift+F1 = Shift+Screen 1 (* on a step)
shift+F1 last
# Ctrl+Z = Shift+Screen 8 = undo
ctrl+Z last print
# Home = Shift+Insert (the block's top)
Home last
# F11 = FX1; Esc in a menu = Cancel
Right Right Right F11 last Escape last menulist
# Space = Play (evaluate), Ctrl+Enter too
Space last ctrl+Return last
# Alt held = Pattern: Alt+1 mutes d1, Shift+Alt alone = hush
down:Left_Alt 1 up:Left_Alt last
shift+Left_Alt last
# Ctrl+L = Song (launch menu), Ctrl+Shift+L = setcps
ctrl+L last Escape ctrl+shift+L last
# Tab = next slot, unmapped keys do nothing
Tab last ctrl+K last
